`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Each work order needs an isolated workspace, intended target platform, immutable input manifest, source and consuming-tool versions, selected operation/options, native diagnostics, output hashes and an explicit acceptance policy. Record documentation versions separately from installed versions."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Keep these states distinct: request accepted; native operation terminal; expected artifacts present; artifacts validated; project saved; fresh process reopened; target-runtime acceptance complete. Record ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"accepted, quality failure, unsupported, infrastructure failure, timeout, cancelled or inconclusive"})," separately. A timeout is not cancellation, a retry is not necessarily idempotent, and an existing file may belong to an earlier run. Cancellation and power-loss durability remain unknown unless a specific source establishes them."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The acceptance and recovery policies below are editorial proposals. Do not repair source assets, replace baselines, normalize audio, alter system network settings, upload packages or publish a build merely to make a check pass. Keep source inputs and failed artifacts. Tool licensing, fonts, media rights, SDK access and deployment authority need their own checks; this document grants none."}),`
