`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Fixed-source corroboration."})," At that commit, ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/scene/resources/resource_format_text.cpp#L1393-L1405",children:"the text-resource loader"})," selects external-dependency reuse for ordinary IGNORE/REUSE/REPLACE and propagates the deep modes; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41/core/io/resource_loader.cpp#L608-L618",children:"the resource loader"})," returns an existing cached resource for REUSE. This corroborates the cache distinction, not every resource-format plugin or the directory-listing warning."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/tutorials/export/exporting_pcks.html",children:"4.4 pack guide"})," also includes scripts among pack contents and documents an additional C# assembly-loading step before mounting a C# mod. Treat a pack as potentially executable content, not merely an inert texture archive; an approved data-pack mount does not establish that its separate assembly was delivered or loaded. This is not a claim that the engine authenticates or sandboxes a mod."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed acceptance."})," Preserve engine/template identity, baseline and ordered pack hashes, expected path collisions, replacement policy and resource-loading/cache policy. Use a project-owned manifest of expected resource paths, types, dependency identities and observable version markers. Record mount results separately from the resources actually returned and the gameplay/rendered result. Validate a fresh process that mounts the intended pack set before loading fixture resources; if hot updates are promised, validate the warm process independently. Do not silently switch to deep replacement in a live game: existing object identity and side effects require their own contract."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Unimplemented fixtures:"})," (1) cache a scene and its external material, mount a patch changing both, then compare default, top-level-ignore and deep-ignore loads against a fresh-process reference; (2) mount two packs with a deliberate path collision in both orders and with replacement disabled; (3) add a new known resource and compare manifest-directed loading with directory-list observations; (4) omit a required dependency or C# assembly and require a distinct activation failure rather than a mount-only pass. Preserve native errors and returned object/dependency markers, not merely screenshots or booleans."]}),`
