`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"CI and rights."})," The committed ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/com.unity.multiplayer.samples.coop/blob/1299ba4fc97d83b634e7d32a86c438ba668d7f9c/.yamato/project-tests.yml",children:"Yamato project-test template"})," filters the BossRoom runtime tests and collects test-result logs, but fetches tools from Unity-internal registries. Its ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/com.unity.multiplayer.samples.coop/blob/1299ba4fc97d83b634e7d32a86c438ba668d7f9c/.yamato/project.metafile",children:"matrix"})," declares editor 6000.0.44, distinct from the project's 6000.0.52f1. The checked configuration is not evidence of a recent successful run or a publicly reproducible CI service. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/com.unity.multiplayer.samples.coop/blob/1299ba4fc97d83b634e7d32a86c438ba668d7f9c/LICENSE.md",children:"license notice"})," points to the Unity Companion License for Unity-dependent projects; do not relabel the sample MIT or infer cross-engine/AI-training rights. Dependency and individual-asset notices need separate review. No account setup, LFS materialization, engine import, compilation or playtest was performed."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed integration fixture, not implemented."})," Freeze a complete materialized project and resolved environment; retain an unmodified baseline. Make one bounded visual/geometry edit to the switch-door encounter, with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ForceOpen"})," disabled and recorded. Build a fresh isolated artifact, retain build/test reports and scene/prefab identities, then compare baseline and candidate through host plus a separate client: enter the level, approach/leave the switch, verify authoritative switch/door state, client animation, collision/navigation traversal and return-to-menu behavior. Capture original frames and correlated events, not just UI-call receipts. Record latency conditions and each client outcome; a scene callback with timed-out clients is incomplete evidence. Keep existing smoke-test results alongside, rather than presenting them as the newly proposed interaction test. This sample supplies connected implementation surfaces; GameMap has not built an agent driver or established reset determinism, independent-process coverage or held-out evaluation results."]}),`
